= Application programming interface — Technical =

An API contract may specify operation names, parameters, types, preconditions, outputs, errors, authentication requirements, versioning, and compatibility behavior. Remote APIs additionally depend on serialization and communication protocols.

== Modeling / implementation cautions ==
* API ≠ Web API only
* API ≠ network protocol necessarily
* interface ≠ implementation

== References ==
* David L. Parnas, information-hiding and modular-interface literature.
* OpenAPI Specification, current specification family, for HTTP API descriptions.
* IETF RFC 9110, for HTTP semantics used by many Web APIs.
